{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1476497-mage-the-awakening-neophyte","id":1476497,"title":"Mage the Awakening Neophyte","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-15T22:07:43-07:00","id":1476497,"title":"Mage the Awakening Neophyte","content":"Would someone be willing to explain the changes made from the original edition to his second edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27330-valairius","name":"Valairius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T22:40:42-07:00","id":1476499,"title":"","content":"Very briefly due to lack of time\u2026<br /> <br /> Lore-wise, mages and their Orders being \u2018descended from the Awakened City\u2019 is now a symbolic declaration rather than a factual statement. Well, it sorta was too starting from some latter 1e supplements iirc, but 2e makes that clearer. We even get to see, in Dark Eras, how disparate mages from the Hellenistic era grouped up into the precursors of modern Orders.<br /> <br /> System-wise, balancing spells/Practices is not done by hard-capping certain effects at higher Arcanum dots, but soft-capping them via Reach. Higher Arcanum dots give you more \u2018free\u2019 Reach. (Eg. You can totally try to mind-control humans at Mind 2, even to self-harm, but good luck trying that consistently if you\u2019re a newbie who got Mind 2 just a few days ago.) Non-free Reach gives you Paradox. Speaking of which, Reach is likely your main source of Paradox, especially with the Covert-Vulgar distinction gone.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Reach being the main source of Paradox also implies that, if you screw up and/or blow up something, most of the time it\u2019s your own damn fault for overestimating yourself and underestimating your challenges. Hubris, indeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 03-16-2022, 01:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T23:00:05-07:00","id":1476500,"title":"","content":"The central changes:<br /> <br /> - The Supernal Realms are more holistically depicted to match their nature in Imperial Mysteries: not a higher dimension or greater plane one can travel to, but a state of being, the symbols and meanings underlying and represented by phenomenal reality. Using the Mage Sight doesn't just reveal an understanding of the phenomenal world through knowledge of the Arcana, but literally opens your eyes to an overlay of the Supernal Realm as it is, intertwined and coexisting with the phenomenal world. A Moros looks at the world undergirded by Stygia and sees the ghosts of regrets and attachments haunting a man. The Obrimos look into the Aether and see the scepter and robes that drape those who wield authority.<br /> <br /> - &quot;Spell aspect&quot; is gone. The risk of Paradox is not connected to how subtle or explicit your spell is in breaching the natural law of the Fallen World. Instead, a Reach mechanic is introduced. The Reach of a mage's spell determines the availability of a number of spell factors, with even the ability to cast a spell without an extended ritual requiring a small modicum of your Reach. There is no limit to how far a mage can push his Reach, but a mage's safe grasp is limited by his understanding. Reaching beyond your understanding has prepared you invites the risk of a Paradox.<br /> <br /> - There is a more overt focus on the notion that mages seek out hidden truths and discover secrets about the world. Anomalies and supernatural mysteries are rife in the world, and a mage's drive to uncover, learn about and harness them is what fuels the accumulation of arcane experience.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T23:00:24-07:00","id":1476501,"title":"","content":"Where can I get a sample or such to review? I'm a real big fan of the original, but I'm willing to read up on this new system of reach and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27330-valairius","name":"Valairius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T23:29:15-07:00","id":1476503,"title":"","content":"Dave Brookshaw posted a number of articles to the Onyx Path blog extensively previewing elements of the new edition in the leadup to its release. You have to dig way back on the Mage: the Awakening tag history to get there, but Addicted to Mysteries on what should be <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/worlds/chroniclesofdarkness/magetheawakening/page/11/\" target=\"_blank\">this page</a> marks the beginning of the series, from which you can read forward.<br /> <br /> (You may see artifacts of the weird intellectual property ping-pong that was going on at the time. CCP, who held ownership at the time, initially did not want the revision of each gameline to be referred to as a &quot;second edition,&quot; so they were initially referred to as &quot;chronicle books&quot; that featured signature chronicle hooks alongside the revision. That's why there's a post &quot;announcing&quot; the second edition a few posts into this development diary of Mage Second Edition.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-16T04:39:28-07:00","id":1476516,"title":"","content":"I think this thread (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/437565-second-edition-development-blogs\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...elopment-blogs</a>) is most useful for finding the blogs, it has all the links on a single page and in order.<br /> <br /> The big difference in mechanics is the change to spell factors. All spells are cast on a basis of single success pulls them off, exceptional success pulls them off with slight benefit, and how far they go is based on penalties to the casting pool. <br /> <br /> Penalties get offset by using yantras, ritual implements with symbolism relevant to the spell you're casting. How many yantras you can use depends on Gnosis.<br /> <br /> And factors default in forms of less convenience, with Reach (and thus Paradox risk at the most basic casting level) necessary to move them to the advanced table. Rituals aren't extended actions to accumulate lots of successes to factors, they're the default for how long it takes to cast a spell. (They <i>can</i> be pushed longer to get up to five bonus dice to the spell)<br /> <br /> Rotes get a couple of good changes out of this; they become normal spell dice pools with a Skill as a Yantra, and they give you as much Reach as if you were a Master. So it's pretty useful even to have 1 dot spells as rotes, because that five free Reach can effectively cover all factors plus boosting the spell effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 03-16-2022, 07:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-19T12:04:40-07:00","id":1476737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rotes get a couple of good changes out of this; they become normal spell dice pools with a Skill as a Yantra, </div> </div> </div>This is a good improvement mechanically. It is no longer the case that the rote dice pool can be smaller than the improvised casting dice pool - it is always a (+skill dots) rote mundra. Whereas in 1e it was Gnosis replaced by attribute+skill, which might be cheaper for less experienced characters to maximise. But at higher Gnosis not so much.<br /> <br /> Praxis were also introduced, which are not present in 1e, and like legacies represent some shaping of a mage's soul.<br /> <br /> A number of non-legacy attainments were codified, taking numerous spell-like abilities from 1e and some other (spread through sidebars) to be more clearly laid out and with common rules (sharing some features with legacy attainments, such as not being spells). <br /> <br /> All good stuff imho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-19T13:04:36-07:00","id":1476743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1476497-mage-the-awakening-neophyte?p=1476516#post1476516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big difference in mechanics is the change to spell factors. All spells are cast on a basis of single success pulls them off, exceptional success pulls them off with slight benefit, and how far they go is based on penalties to the casting pool.<br /> <br /> Penalties get offset by using yantras, ritual implements with symbolism relevant to the spell you're casting. How many yantras you can use depends on Gnosis.</div> </div> </div> </div>For clarity, this is not completely new so much as a rearranging of defaults \u2014 Yantras are significantly comprised of various bonuses to spellcasting from 1e (including sacraments), and spell factors working as they do in 2e is essentially just universalizing 1e's system for guaranteeing higher spell factors on instant-cast spells, down to the scaling of the penalties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-19T17:46:25-07:00","id":1476755,"title":"","content":"I'd say that the thing that does come out as a major change is altering primary factor. In First Edition, it depended on how many successes you rolled, so you couldn't exactly fine tune it and penalties to improve other factors probably came at the expense of it. In Second Edition, primary factor defaults to a level equal to Arcanum rating, and can be lowered at will and raised still further with penalties, but you're still guaranteed a decent result and free up space to expand additional factors.<br /> <br /> There are a bunch of other things that get cleaned up. Rather than being a case of either adding another penalty to the casting pool or rolling a trait against its result (which is which being a tad arbitrary), resisting spells is a streamlined matter of &quot;Potency needs to exceed Stamina, Composure or Resolve&quot;, sympathetic casting cuts down on the number of levels of connection and makes it a resistance to overcome rather than a penalty, as well as temporal sympathy being made more its own thing... oh, aimed spells were revised significantly, so that rather than being &quot;sometimes spells can be used as projectiles&quot; they're an option for when you don't Reach from touch to sensory range, being able to throw the spell whatever it is (offset by it being necessary to make it an area spell).<br /> <br /> Legacy powers were revised into something more systematized. For one thing, they get five Attainments rather than three, so there's earlier access and more ongoing progression. When Attainments are meant to have powers resembling spells, they're modelled more directly off of those spells, so not so much odd cases like the Bearers of the Eternal Voice getting their Mind dots as automatic social successes. The most significant thing is that the power of Attainments have to be fully accounted for in the Reach you'd get for an Arcanum rating, with no option to go beyond it (as well as generally set factors, since they're not rolled to activate). This can lead to cases where a high level Attainment confers a lower level of spell; if you want Psychic Domination that can be used instantly, at sensory range and provides anything goes level command, that needs to be a fifth Attainment even though it's a 2 dot spell because you need Mind 5 to provide all the Reach that needs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-17T02:31:51-07:00","id":1479003,"title":"","content":"Been out of commission for a slight minute.<br /> <br /> The next question is how has everyone reacted to the new MtA 2ed? The entire spellcasting has been revamped. How does everyone feel about the changesmand adaptations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27330-valairius","name":"Valairius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T21:42:12-07:00","id":1484085,"title":"","content":"I love the new MtA 2ed. The only thing I might want to tweak is Wisdom but that's a totally new topic and others have posted their ideas about that. Wisdom is fine in 2ed, I think it could be better used but whatever.<br /> <br /> The spellcasting is more clear, as is paradox. I love the new tilts and conditions, it makes it easier to adjudicate effects in a consistent manner. I love beats which encourages Role Playing. I like how most spells can deal damage, heal, enhance traits, etc. This allow players to be more creative instead of needing to get Life to heal or Matter to make equipment. <br /> <br /> Bottom line is there's no hesitation to switch from 1ed to 2ed. Anything else you'd like to know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13187-kuldirongaze","name":"Kuldirongaze","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}